Description: CVE-2026-67213 - nanoid customAlphabet/customRandom infinite loop on size <= 0
 When customAlphabet/customRandom (and the async variants) are called with a
 size of 0 or a negative number, the generator never reaches the exit condition
 (id.length === size), causing an unbounded loop that exhausts CPU/memory. This
 backports upstream fix f9d13f150847d117877adee3460a46eceb0cf49b to short-circuit
 and return an empty string for size <= 0, syncing the 0-size behaviour. Test-file
 hunks from upstream are omitted because the published npm tarball ships no test/ dir.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/ai/nanoid/commit/f9d13f150847d117877adee3460a46eceb0cf49b
